{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_33d1cf01a6bfcad0d9c4df4ef23da1c6e7254a43a78d348bba914b5822ef67f0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are asked to open an issue or submit a pull request, and a ROADMAP.md lists priorities for community contributions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44effe643c218af7393a449baa3e734de40ff4ad2bbc1e8cba317ffc379566d0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workflow bindings are configured in `~/.opendev/settings.json` with keys like `model_provider`, `model`, `model_thinking_provider`, and `model_thinking`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_45f6186c1729a04a722d29291a00a6a37b21a80b82ea1f4b40ce4e9552b2e878"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports a benchmark comparing OpenDev 0.1.4 startup (4.3 ms), peak memory (9.4 MB), and install size (18 MB) against Codex, Claude Code, and OpenCode on macOS ARM64 using hyperfine and /usr/bin/time."},{"claim_ids":["clm_503fccdc1b8c9488d684ace2158f9b123df837d07cd7016bbd32d16ffbc7ad8b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers an interactive TUI (`opendev`), a Web UI (`opendev run ui`), single-prompt mode (`-p`), session resume (`--continue`), and an interactive `opendev config setup` for provider/model binding."},{"claim_ids":["clm_587ad963f0b29c88ef84f12dcef9d4ea5191f60cd22ff4e50b88e648d835bf9d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Five workflow slots are defined: Normal (execution), Thinking (reasoning), Compact (context summarization), Critique (self-critique), and VLM (vision), each bindable to any configured LLM."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a37a5639b9500601d35921738382ebbdd7c5d31c459de9de01bc5a720a5aa074"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workflow slots have documented fallback behavior: Thinking and Compact fall back to Normal, Critique falls back to Thinking, and VLM falls back to Normal when the model lacks vision."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a7ea034be18177b69b9c1a56b4d0f55a061c21db4ad2a8403a5d5abee745b940"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent supports nine LLM providers: OpenAI, Anthropic, Fireworks, Google, Groq, Mistral, DeepInfra, OpenRouter, and Azure OpenAI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b679802c5a694a0347f7891060e029565b37b2bd707da0f957abf9949251ecab"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An agent fleet can launch multiple sub-agents in parallel, each with its own LLM binding, context window, and tool access, aggregating results back into the session."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c03e2811bd10f1ede30152f87f4be947acc9fd89fca916623a976007e2ac1de8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Building from source requires Rust 1.94 or later, and the runtime uses Tokio for async parallelism."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ccb040ffd3a9244a0ac84fa03356277cae4e88b35310173b5b6d1587cafca615"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MCP integration provides dynamic tool discovery with subcommands such as `opendev mcp list`, `mcp add`, and `mcp enable/disable`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e39232c09512d5721611cc3d38e7b02fe3cdee244f6f01f43e6aa9f586f84c0b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors build with `cargo build --workspace`, run `cargo test --workspace`, and use cargo check, clippy, and fmt; the Web UI frontend is built with `npm ci && npm run build`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f4ae9d69bbb3a124e5d977d19aab6973e9e30cd266f9137d3d007de153cf832d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"OpenDev is described as an open-source, terminal-native coding agent built as a compound AI system of agents and workflows, each independently bound to a user-configured model."}],"claim_ids":["clm_33d1cf01a6bfcad0d9c4df4ef23da1c6e7254a43a78d348bba914b5822ef67f0","clm_44effe643c218af7393a449baa3e734de40ff4ad2bbc1e8cba317ffc379566d0","clm_45f6186c1729a04a722d29291a00a6a37b21a80b82ea1f4b40ce4e9552b2e878","clm_503fccdc1b8c9488d684ace2158f9b123df837d07cd7016bbd32d16ffbc7ad8b","clm_587ad963f0b29c88ef84f12dcef9d4ea5191f60cd22ff4e50b88e648d835bf9d","clm_a37a5639b9500601d35921738382ebbdd7c5d31c459de9de01bc5a720a5aa074","clm_a7ea034be18177b69b9c1a56b4d0f55a061c21db4ad2a8403a5d5abee745b940","clm_b679802c5a694a0347f7891060e029565b37b2bd707da0f957abf9949251ecab","clm_c03e2811bd10f1ede30152f87f4be947acc9fd89fca916623a976007e2ac1de8","clm_ccb040ffd3a9244a0ac84fa03356277cae4e88b35310173b5b6d1587cafca615","clm_e39232c09512d5721611cc3d38e7b02fe3cdee244f6f01f43e6aa9f586f84c0b","clm_f4ae9d69bbb3a124e5d977d19aab6973e9e30cd266f9137d3d007de153cf832d"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b","id":"pg_21adcbb189f153bca255a3cf0a9cdd0b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/opendev-to-opendev-readme-md-d32c660e4eed-a3cf0a9cdd0b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_533b5a956b54509da8dde81369676b2e"],"title":"opendev-to/opendev/README.md @ d32c660e4eed","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9a1036f5d484555b51b691904b4ff8b"}
